            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0782" n="766" xml:id="pg766"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 55D128: Black Book, Tab 127: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United Nations Command</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ridgway</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Joint
                        Chiefs of Staff </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-08-01T21:21:00+10:00">1 August 1951—9:21
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>C–68130. “This msg in 5 parts. Subj: Armistice Conference at Kaesong 1 Aug
                    51.</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Part 1</hi>.</p>
                <p>“Summary:</p>
                <p>“Meeting consisted of continuation of rebuttals, and reaffirmations of own
                    positions by each side. No new thoughts offered by enemy. Adm Joy offered
                    several opportunities to Nam Il to engage in map study, and to propose zones
                    based on lines other than 38th parallel. Nam Il exhibited no interest. Adm Joy
                    repeated several times statement that as a basis for establishing demilitarized
                    zone, 38th parallel was totally unacceptable to United Nations Comd. Nam Il held
                    rigidly to 38th as only solution.</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Part 2</hi>.</p>
                <p>“Progress: None.</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Part 3</hi>.</p>
                <p>“Attitudes: No significant change.</p>
                <p>[Here follows Part 4, an abridged version of the transcript of the day’s
                    proceedings.]</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Part 5</hi>. Conclusion: The UNC delegation feels that: <list>
                        <item>“1. Conference is still in a deadlock over the issue of 38
                            Parallel.</item>
                        <item>“2. No evidence that enemy is likely to shift from his psn reference
                            38 Parallel.</item>
                        <item>“3. It is obvious that Nam Il is building up the record. Whether this
                            is for purpose of defending a request for recess or is an attempt to
                            place the onus on us for a break in the negotiations is not known. I
                            concur.”</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
            </div>
